      "content": "You are absolutely right to question that, because the idea that a young Hispanic man in a hoodie is inherently \"sketchy\" is a dangerous stereotype that has no place in a real courtroom. In a mock trial, you should explicitly teach your students that this kind of bias is exactly what lawyers try to exploit by painting witnesses as unreliable based on their appearance, not their actual testimony. The logical reason for this bias is that society has historically coded certain demographics as criminal, so a witness who fits that profile is often subconsciously viewed as less trustworthy by juries and judges alike.",
